+---
+id: dl-005-cancellation-refund-full-before-start-prorated-during-zero-after-equipment-released-immediately
+type: decision-log
+title: "Cancellation refund: full before start, prorated during, zero after, equipment released immediately"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Context
+
+`cancel(bookingId, at)` had to return a `refund`, but the request didn't say how much of the total to
+give back, only that cancellation happens "at the time `at`" — so `at` had to matter to the amount, not
+just be a timestamp for the record (which, per the determinism directive, also means `cancel` takes it as
+an explicit argument rather than reading the wall clock itself).
+
+## Decision
+
+- **Refund policy**: linear to how much of the booked period is still unused at `at`, compared against
+  the booking's `start`/`end` (already in ms, needing no new period semantics beyond dl-001/dl-004's
+  `RentalPeriod`):
+  - `at <= start`: full refund (nothing consumed yet).
+  - `at >= end`: no refund (the whole period is behind it).
+  - otherwise: `round(total * (end - at) / (end - start))`, the same "round to the nearest cent" rule
+    `priceForDays` already uses (dl-003), since `total` is integer cents everywhere else in the service.
+  - This applies uniformly to day and hour bookings alike, since it only compares timestamps, not units.
+- **Equipment released immediately, not at `at`**: cancelling removes the booking from its item's entry in
+  `bookingsByItem` right away, so `book`/`availability` treat the slot as free as soon as `cancel` returns,
+  regardless of whether `at` is in the past, present, or future relative to the booking.
+- **Cancel-once tracked separately from release**: a `cancelledBookingIds` set (keyed by booking id) is
+  checked before refunding, so a second `cancel` call throws instead of silently recomputing a refund
+  (and instead of a vague "unknown booking" error, which would conflate "never existed" with "already
+  cancelled"). A new `bookingsById` map was added for O(1) lookup by id, since `bookingsByItem` is only
+  keyed by item id.
+- **`at` is validated the same way other date strings in the service are**: an unparseable `at` throws
+  `'at must be a valid ISO-8601 UTC time'`, mirroring `resolvePeriod`'s existing message for `start`/`end`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A customer who cancels before the rental starts gets a full refund; one who cancels mid-rental gets a
+  partial refund proportional to time remaining; one who cancels after it's over gets nothing. No
+  cancellation fee or minimum-refund floor was introduced, since the request didn't ask for one.
+- Because release is immediate and unconditional on `at`, cancelling with an `at` *inside* an already-past
+  period still frees the item for new bookings right away; the service does not model "the booking already
+  happened, so the slot was already free again" — only explicit `cancel` calls free a slot early.
+- A future request for a cancellation fee or a non-linear refund curve would change `refundFor` alone,
+  since it's the single point where refund amount is computed.
