@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+---
+id: task-005-allow-cancelling-a-booking
+type: task
+title: "Allow cancelling a booking"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental service: it cancels the booking at the time `at` and returns
+`{ bookingId, refund }`, the amount given back to the customer. A cancelled booking no longer holds its
+equipment, and a booking can only be cancelled once.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added failing tests first (red) in `src/index.test.ts`: full refund when cancelled before the booking
+  starts, no refund when cancelled at or after it ends, a prorated refund for a cancellation during the
+  booking, the item becoming available again (and re-bookable) after cancellation, an unknown booking id
+  throwing, cancelling twice throwing, and an invalid `at` throwing.
+- Implemented `cancel(bookingId, at)` in `src/index.ts` (green): looks up the booking by id (a new
+  `bookingsById` map, populated alongside the existing per-item `bookingsByItem` map in `book()`), rejects
+  an unknown id or a booking already in the new `cancelledBookingIds` set, validates `at` as a parseable
+  ISO-8601 time, then removes the booking from its item's `bookingsByItem` entry (so it stops blocking
+  `book`/`availability` overlap checks) and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`.
+- Added a `refundFor(booking, at)` helper and the `Cancellation` exported type; see
+  dl-005-cancellation-refund-full-before-start-prorated-during-zero-after-equipment-released-immediately
+  for the refund policy decision, since the request didn't specify one.
+- Added `cancel` to the `RentalService` interface with a doc comment, per the documentation directive.
+- All 37 tests pass (`node --test`); no new dependency was added.
